<title>FRANCE: Total says has promising Angola tests.</title>
<headline>Total says has promising Angola tests.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil group Total said it had made promising tests on the D14-2X well on block 14 in deep water off the coast of Cabinda in Angola.</p>
<p>It said the well had a cumulative crude flow of around 7,500 barrels per day in a water depth of 405 metres (1,330 ft).</p>
<p>Total has a 20 percent interest in block 14 while Chevron has 31 percent, Angola's Sonangol 20 percent, AGIP of Italy 20 percent and Portugal's Petrogal nine percent.</p>
</text>
